reen.\n\n### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n\nLooking at the code structure, there are some opportunities:\n\n1. **`processScenario` is long**: It mixes iteration, validation, quote handling, and claim handling. Could a well-named function for the claim result help?\n2. **Claim always returns `{ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 }`** — this is a placeholder. Since there are no claim calculation tests yet, this is fine.\n\n### Rule 3: No Duplication\n\nKey duplication I see:\n1. **The `|| 0` pattern**: `componentCounts.get(item.type) || 0` uses a JavaScript idiom, but there's no duplication of this across the file.\n2. **The for-of validation loops**: `validateItemTypes`, `validateClaimDamages`, and `checkAllItemTypesValid` all iterate over arrays and throw errors. There's mild conceptual repetition but the logic differs enough.\n\nActually, I see a structural issue: **`handleQuote` does two things**: computes a premium AND registers a policy. These are separate concerns.\n\n### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n\nLooking at the code:\n- `handleQuote` computes premium AND updates `policies` — but these are done in one function. The naming doesn't reveal the policy registration side effect.\n- Claim result always returns `{ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 }` which is fine (placeholder).\n\n### Chosen Refactoring\n\nThe clearest improvement I see is: **the `computeBasePremium` function has a nested conditional that handles two separate cases (components vs non-components) inside one loop. This could be made more intention-revealing by separating \"counting components\" from \"summing non-component items\".**\n\nBut wait — that would introduce more loops and increase mass. Let me think about what actually reduces mass while improving clarity...\n\nActually, looking more carefully, I think the best refactoring is a naming one:\n\n**`COMPONENT_TYPES` → `BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES`** — this better reveals the intent. \"Component\" is a domain term but \"block pricing types\" tells you WHY the set exists (it's for block pricing, not just identifying components).\n\nAlso, `validateClaimDamages` has the same loop+conditional pattern as `checkAllItemTypesValid` — they both iterate and check with separate error messages. But extracting a common helper would add abstraction mass without real clarity gain.\n\nLet me go with the naming improvement.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Implement Refact"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7736db5d9c914d7a9014451a","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"oldText":"const COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);","newText":"const BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);"},{"oldText":"    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {","newText":"    if (BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES.has(item.type)) {"}],"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":564,"output":3130,"cacheRead":9728,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13422,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784948997890,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ac2dcdca-7d4e-4fd3-b0be-b8f76f981cd1","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7736db5d9c914d7a9014451a","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  57   // Group components by type for block pricing\n  58   const componentCounts: Map<string, number> = new Map();\n  59   let basePremium = 0;\n  60   for (const item of items) {\n- 61     if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n+ 61     if (BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n  62       componentCounts.set(item.type, (componentCounts.get(item.type) || 0) + 1);\n  63     } else {\n  64       basePremium += getItemBasePremium(item);\n  65     }\n     ...\n  73   }\n  74   return basePremium;\n  75 }\n  76 \n- 77 const COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n+ 77 const BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n  78 \n  79 const BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  80   sword: 100,\n  81   amulet: 60,\n     ...","patch":"--- src/claim-office.ts\n+++ src/claim-office.ts\n@@ -57,9 +57,9 @@\n   // Group components by type for block pricing\n   const componentCounts: Map<string, number> = new Map();\n   let basePremium = 0;\n   for (const item of items) {\n-    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n+    if (BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n       componentCounts.set(item.type, (componentCounts.get(item.type) || 0) + 1);\n     } else {\n       basePremium += getItemBasePremium(item);\n     }\n@@ -73,9 +73,9 @@\n   }\n   return basePremium;\n }\n \n-const COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n+const BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n \n const BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n   sword: 100,\n   amulet: 60,\n","firstChangedLine":61},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949009027},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me verify tests"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ae7a1231e59240df9690ebbf","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-04-28_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro && pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":390,"output":123,"cacheRead":13056,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13569,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949009028,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-9599e4e0-e0e6-46b3-97c3-46a6229f49b2","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ae7a1231e59240df9690ebbf","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-04-28_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-04-28_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (43 tests | 30 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  13 passed | 30 todo (43)\n   Start at  03:10:10\n   Duration  180ms (transform 32ms, setup 0ms, collect 30ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 52ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949010736},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 13 tests still pass. Now let me verify the final state"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8cf88b1c08f74546836bc782","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":472,"output":64,"cacheRead":13312,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13848,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949010737,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-12a09513-c975-45a9-88f2-5a39469c42e6","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8cf88b1c08f74546836bc782","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type Scenario = {\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[];\n  };\n}\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  validateItemTypes(scenario);\n  const policies: Set<string>[] = [];\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      quoteCount++;\n      results.push(handleQuote(step, policies));\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      validateClaimDamages(step, policies);\n      results.push({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 });\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n}\n\nfunction handleQuote(step: QuoteStep, policies: Set<string>[]): StepResult {\n  const items = step.items;\n  const coveredItemTypes = new Set(items.map(i => i.type));\n  policies.push(coveredItemTypes);\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return { premium: PROCESSING_FEE };\n  }\n  const basePremium = computeBasePremium(items);\n  return { premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE };\n}\n\nfunction computeBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  // Group components by type for block pricing\n  const componentCounts: Map<string, number> = new Map();\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts.set(item.type, (componentCounts.get(item.type) || 0) + 1);\n    } else {\n      basePremium += getItemBasePremium(item);\n    }\n  }\n  // Apply block pricing for components\n  for (const [type, count] of componentCounts) {\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / 3);\n    const remainder = count % 3;\n    basePremium += blocks * 60;  // 60 G per block of 3\n    basePremium += remainder * getItemBasePremium({ type } as Item);\n  }\n  return basePremium;\n}\n\nconst BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nfunction getItemBasePremium(item: Item): number {\n  return BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n}\n\ntype StepResult = { premium?: number; payout?: number; remainingCap?: number };\n\nfunction validateItemTypes(scenario: Scenario): void {\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      checkAllItemTypesValid(step.items.map(i => i.type));\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      checkAllItemTypesValid(step.incident.damages.map(d => d.itemType));\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateClaimDamages(step: ClaimStep, policies: Set<string>[]): void {\n  const policy = policies[step.policy];\n  for (const damage of step.incident.damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(\"Negative damage amount\");\n    }\n    if (!policy.has(damage.itemType)) {\n      throw new Error(`${damage.itemType} not covered by policy`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction checkAllItemTypesValid(types: string[]): void {\n  for (const type of types) {\n    if (!VALID_ITEM_TYPES.has(type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst VALID_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949011545},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\nThe mass is almost identical — only the constant name changed from `COMPONENT_TYPES` to `BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES`. The constant count and binding count are unchanged:\n\n```\nTotal Mass = 186 (unchanged)\n```\n\nThe mass didn't decrease because this was purely a naming improvement, not a structural one. But the name now better reveals intent.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Naming**: Renamed `COMPONENT_TYPES` → `BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES` (Rule 2: Reveals Intent)\n- **Mass**: 186 → 186 (unchanged — naming-only change)\n- **Rule 2 impact**: `BLOCK_PRICING_TYPES` directly says these types get block pricing, rather than the domain term \"component\" which is less specific about the pricing mechanism\n\n**Why this and not more:**\n- No structural duplication exists at this stage (13 tests in, still early)\n- The `claim` side is intentionally a placeholder (`{ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 }`) since no claim calculation tests are active yet\n- No unnecessary abstractions to remove\n- Code structure follows the natural domain breakdown: validation, quote computation, policy registr